        "results_interpretation": "Based on the pooled analysis of six studies, quercetin exposure is associated with a substantially lower odds of breast cancer incidence, as indicated by a summary effect size of 0.54. The 95% confidence interval (0.38, 0.79) suggests this association is statistically significant and likely to reflect a true relationship rather than chance. However, the high heterogeneity found in this meta-analysis (I\u00b2 = 82.68%) indicates notable variability among the included studies, which may arise from differences in populations, study designs, or exposure assessment methods. This suggests caution in interpretation, as the strength and nature of the observed association may differ across various contexts."
